FINDING (in scope, FAIL basis): C1's fix broke the pre-existing LIVE preview
of "(~X% expected)" whenever an account's allocation is edited while
investment_return is 0 — a second, untested call path into the same display
function that the fix did not account for.
- `updateAccountBonds()` (whatif-rate-assumptions.js) fires on every
  `oninput` of the six per-account stock/cash percent fields
  (tax_deferred_stock_percent, tax_deferred_cash_percent, roth_*, taxable_*;
  wired via `oninput="updateAccountBonds('td'|'roth'|'taxable')"` in
  rate-assumptions.html) and, when `investment_return` is 0, calls
  `updateInvestmentReturnDisplay(0)` — the SAME function C1 changed to read
  only `display.dataset.expectedReturn` (the last SERVER-rendered figure,
  static HTML, never updated by JS). This call site is untouched by the
  attempt-5 diff's comments/reasoning (which discusses only the
  investment-return slider's own drag) and has zero test coverage (`grep -n
  updateAccountBonds web/static/js/whatif-rate-assumptions.test.cjs` = 0
  matches); the oracle's E8 also never touches an allocation field (it only
  sets `#qa-investment-return` to 3 then back to 0 with allocation
  untouched, so `data-expected-return` never goes stale in that check).
- Demonstrated live on the real server (fixture: investment_return=0,
  tax_deferred_percent=83.037%, tax_deferred_stock/cash=70.5/2.25%,
  roth_percent=0, taxable_stock/cash=99.5/0%; served text/attr both "6.2"):
  typing "0" into the tax-deferred stock-percent field (real keyboard
  events, Playwright) leaves the in-card display frozen at "Using asset
  allocation (~6.2% expected)" — byte-identical to before the keystroke —
  for as long as the field holds focus. Only after Tab (blur -> `change` ->
  the form's existing 500ms-debounced `hx-post /whatif/settings` -> OOB
  swap) does it update, to "(~4.5% expected)" — which I independently
  computed by hand from `GetExpectedReturnFromAllocation`'s own published
  formula/constants for the new allocation (0/97.75/2.25 stock/bond/cash at
  weight 0.830371…) and confirmed matches exactly. So the save/render path
  itself is correct; only the LIVE window before blur shows a stale figure.
- Confirmed this is a NEW regression, not pre-existing: ran the identical
  keystroke against a real master (643fa54) build on the same fixture.
  Master's `updateInvestmentReturnDisplay(0)` still calls
  `calculateExpectedReturnFromAllocation()` (unchanged there), which reads
  the live DOM values on every call — master's display updated IMMEDIATELY
  on the same keystroke, to "(~5.9% expected)" (itself imperfect, per
  WS1.4's O1 `||60`/`||10` fallback finding on OTHER zero fields, but
  genuinely live/responsive). Attempt 5 traded a wrong-but-live number for a
  right-but-frozen one on this trigger, and the freeze is real: confirmed no
  other code path writes `dataset.expectedReturn` (`grep -n
  "dataset.expectedReturn\|data-expected-return" web/static/js/*.js` finds
  only the one read site introduced by this attempt).
- Root cause: C1's remedy (always trust the server's baked attribute, never
  recompute) was scoped by the contract/worker to "dragging investment
  return to 0," but `updateInvestmentReturnDisplay(0)` is shared by a SECOND,
  independent trigger (editing allocation while investment_return is
  already 0) that the fix silently disabled without replacing with anything
  live. This is the split-classification/shared-function class CLAUDE.md
  flags: one function, two triggers, the fix addressed one and broke the
  other's existing (if imperfect) correctness property — "Live updates on
  user input must produce exactly the string the server would render"
  (R-FMT') is violated for the allocation-edit trigger: the string shown
  during the edit is NOT what the server would render for the just-typed,
  about-to-be-saved allocation (it's the server's OLD figure).
- Remedy checked for plausibility (not misdiagnosed): a fix that recomputes
  from the live account fields when THIS EXACT call originates from an
  allocation edit (or fixes the `||60`/`||10` fallback bug in
  `calculateExpectedReturnFromAllocation` and keeps using it for this
  trigger, reserving the server-attribute read only for the
  investment-return control's own drag) would restore live behavior without
